# Deliberate test fixtures, not credentials.
#
# Both are flagged correctly — they really are a private key and a JWT — so the
# right answer is to say why they are here rather than to weaken the rule.
# Anything that appears in this file should be provably worthless outside the
# test suite; if it is not, it does not belong in the repository at all.

# A 2048-bit RSA key generated for the test suite's mock identity provider. It
# signs tokens that only `tests/http_auth.rs` and `src/http/auth.rs` ever
# verify, against an issuer that exists only in those tests. Committing it
# keeps the tests hermetic and fast; generating one per run would add a
# keygen dependency and seconds to every build.
src/http/testdata/test-key.pem:private-key:1

# An unsigned `alg: none` token, hardcoded so the test proves such a token is
# rejected. It carries no signature and no real claims — that is the point.
src/http/auth.rs:jwt:353
